[38;5;252m[1m## How it was tested[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Both libraries are loaded with [38;5;10mlibloading[0m and called only through [38;5;10mdlsym[0m, so the [38;5;10m#[no_mangle][0m wrappers are under test. Comparisons cover the returned [38;5;10malert_data[0m field by field, the entire 440-byte [38;5;10mfile_queue[0m, the [38;5;10mFILE*[0m offset/EOF/error state after every call, stderr bytes, and child-process exit status for the [38;5;10mexit(EXIT_FAILURE)[0m paths.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Reaching the harder error branches needed some plumbing: a pipe-backed [38;5;10mFILE*[0m for the push-back [38;5;10mfseek[0m failure, a FIFO with a held-open writer so [38;5;10mfopen[0m succeeds but [38;5;10mfseek[0m returns [38;5;10mESPIPE[0m (the only way [38;5;10mdriver[0m ever prints [3mFile queue initialization failed[23m), and a stream whose descriptor is closed behind its back for the [38;5;10mfstat[0m failure.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Confidence in the result[0m[0m
[0m[0m
A green suite on the first pass is weak evidence, so I mutation-tested the harness: six deliberate bugs injected into the Rust ([38;5;10mSRCIP_BEGIN_SZ[0m 8→7, [38;5;10mstrncpy[0m length 3→4, an altered [38;5;10mos_strdup[0m message, a non-wrapping [38;5;10mfseek[0m push-back, prefix length 33→32, [38;5;10matoi(p) as c_uint[0m → [38;5;10munsigned_abs()[0m) were all caught. The last one was caught only by [38;5;10mrow21_numeric_shapes[0m, so I extended the fuzz corpus with negative and overflowing numerics.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
I also found [38;5;10mfuzz_random_bytes[0m was vacuous — 6000 cases all comparing [38;5;10mNULL == NULL[0m. It now splices real alert lines into the soup, and every fuzz test asserts a minimum number of cases actually parsed an alert.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
